WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.807
Numerical datasets often contain missing values.

00:00:03.807 --> 00:00:10.727
NumPy commonly represents a missing floating-point value as NaN.

00:00:10.727 --> 00:00:13.434
In code, you will see N P dot nan.

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:19.819
A regular mean can return NaN if the array contains a missing value.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:26.329
NumPy also provides missing-aware functions, such as nan mean and nan median,

00:00:26.329 --> 00:00:30.284
that ignore those missing values during the calculation.

00:00:30.284 --> 00:00:34.494
This does not mean we should always ignore missing data.

00:00:34.494 --> 00:00:38.574
The correct decision depends on why the value is missing.

00:00:38.574 --> 00:00:46.589
The important point is to recognize missing values and choose a method deliberately rather than letting them silently

00:00:46.589 --> 00:00:47.325
affect the result.
